    "badge": "Expedition Choice",
    "description": "The city of Grozny today resembles one of the European cities. You will not find traces of the events of the 90s here.\r\nNow the look of the city is a combination of a new architectural trend with the preservation of historically significant architectural buildings, which are the decoration of the capital of the Chechen Republic. Many mosques against the backdrop of modern skyscrapers make you forget that you are in Russia.\r\n\r\nDuration: 12 hours.\r\n\r\nDeparture from city Nalchik at 9:00.\r\n\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Memorial of memory and glory in Ingushetia\"]\r\n\r\nAnd the first stop is the Memorial of Memory and Glory in Ingushetia.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1698,1697,1696,1695,1692,1667\"]\r\n\r\nThe center of the memorial composition is a building of nine traditional watchtowers, symbolically entangled with barbed wire. It houses the exposition of the museum of victims of political repression. The number of towers is not accidental. Nine is the number of deported nations. The memorial is dedicated to two topics - the participation of the Ingush people in the Great World War 2 and the deportation of the Ingush people in 1944. The complex impresses with its scale, well-groomedness and variety of monuments.\r\n\r\nOn the territory of the memorial, there is an impressive equestrian monument to the Ingush Regiment of the Wild Division, a monument to Lieutenant Umatgirey Artaganovich Barkhanoev, a steam locomotive with a wagon (this was the one in which the deportation was carried out), as well as a military exposition.\r\n\r\nStaying time: 25 min.\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"Tower of Concord\"]\r\n\r\nOur next stop is the city of Magas in Republic Ingushetia. Its visiting card is the Tower of Concord - the highest observation tower in the North Caucasus. It was erected in the style of a medieval Ingush tower enlarged four times. Height - 100 meters.\r\n\r\nAccording to legend, in ancient times, the tallest “Tower of the Country” stood on the site of the modern tower, which was a symbol of freedom for the inhabitants of the ancient settlement. The enemies who attacked the village destroyed everything alive and completely dismantled the tower. Tradition says that only the people, united by a single spirit of creation and a common goal, will be able to build a new tower on the same place higher than the previous one.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1752,1753,1754,1755,1756,1757\"]\r\n\r\nAt an altitude of 85 m, there is an observation deck with a stunning panora",
