    "description": "Verkhnyaya Balkaria is an amazing place, nestled in the mountains and combining the true beauty of pristine nature, the grandeur of mountain peaks and the originality of ancient sights. Everyone should visit it at least once and see everything with their own eyes. Here everything around is saturated with uniqueness - air, mountains, ancient history. A small village high in the mountains with a special climate, local people, way of life and unhurried pace of life. Everything here is incredibly sincere and simple. The atmosphere is amazing, the air is fresh, the scenery is picturesque, the local food is delicious, and the peace and quiet is soothing. It is here that the true history of the entire Balkar people is hidden.\r\n\r\nOn the way to the famous village, we will visit a very popular tourist place - Blue Lake. The complex of blue lakes is a unique natural phenomenon of the republic, and of the whole country. Located in an incredibly picturesque place, among the greenery of forests and mountain peaks. Nature is calming and multifaceted.\r\n\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"BLUE LAKES\"]\r\n\r\nLower Blue Lake is the deepest karst lake in Russia and the second deepest in the world! There are no tributaries to the lake, but a stream flows out. The water in it is cold, about 9 degrees all year round and in all levels. Fish is not found in it due to the low salinity of the water. The water is blue and completely transparent, the smooth water surface reflects the sky and the surrounding landscape. Time seems to freeze here, and the feeling of reality just leaves. The lake is beautiful in any weather and season. Shrouded in secrets and legends. A special charm to this place is given by a pair of swans living here. Around the lake there is a colorful local market with many souvenirs and handicrafts. Many small cafes have also been organized, a diving center has been built.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1800,1801,1802\"]\r\n\r\nAfter taking memorable photos and admiring the landscapes, we will go further to the Cherek gorge, along which we can take a fascinating walk and listen to the guide's stories about the history of this place.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1804,1805,1806\"]\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"Cherek Gorge\"]\r\nOur way will pass along the serpentine, up to the tunnel in the Cherek gorge. One of the most breathtaking stages of the tour is a walk along the old road, which is carved right into the sheer cliff. It is here that the power of nature ",
