    "description": "[timeline][timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Blue lakes\"]\r\n\r\nWe make our first stop at Lower Blue Lake, one of the most popular place for tourists. It is attractive not only for its unique beauty, but also for its convenient location, close proximity to the highway.\r\n\r\nThe name of the lake is Tserik-Kol or Cherek-Kel. For a long time, the exact depth of the lake remained a mystery. Even such a famous scuba diver as Jacques Yves Cousteau did not establish it reliably. To date, it is believed that its depth is 360 meters, but not all the crevices by the bathyscaphe can descend, so this is not the final size. In terms of depth, Lower Blue Lake is the second karst lake in the world. Karst is a hole in the rock that looks like a well.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1801,1802,1800\"]\r\n\r\nThe color of the lake is unusually beautiful and changeable. From soft blue in clear weather to azure. The water surface is calm, as if the lake is frozen. The water is clean, completely transparent, the walls of the lake are visible. The place is full of mysterious and enigmatic beauty.\r\n\r\nOn the shore of the lake, the locals staged a real market. Here you can buy souvenirs, jewelry, toys made from natural materials, knitted items and much more, which tourists buy with pleasure as a keepsake of the trip.\r\n\r\nWe will spend an hour on the lake. If desired, we can also organize lunch here. Next, we are driving for the Cherek gorge.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1859,1860,1861\"]\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"Cherek canyon\"]\r\nOur way will follow on serpentine, up to a tunnel in the Cherek Gorge. One of the most striking stages of the tour is a walk along the old road, which is carved right into the sheer cliff. It is here that the power of nature and the elements, the power of the river's work, are clearly felt. After the tunnel, the road to the Zylki fortress begins. A unique fortress leaning against a sheer cliff like some kind of bird's nest. It is from here that the huge ancient defensive system begins, which was built back in the Middle Ages, the tower of the Balkarovs, Amir Khan, Kurnayat, and other amazing monuments of the past. We will plunge into the times of wars and battles, brave men and traitors, hear many stories and legends about the owners of these places.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1846,1812,1852\"]\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"3\" title=\"Chegem waterfalls\"]\r\n\r\nVisiting card of the Kabardino-Balkaria Republic. The waterfalls, comfortably located in the g",
