    "description": "Chegem is a strong, capricious, powerful, noisy mountain river forming narrow canyon Chegem. On a hot summer day, it is especially pleasant to walk near it. The air is saturated with moisture, you want to breathe deeply. Incredibly beautiful and diverse waterfalls - jets of water flow from the very rocks, from the very top, as if from the very bowels of the earth. The gorge captivates tourists at first sight! Just imagine - on one side there is a steep rock, on the other a stormy river, and streams of water break out of the rocks! And with what power! They create a wall of water. Chegem waterfalls are also called Weeping waterfalls. It really does look like the rocks are crying. In winter, the waterfalls turn into a magical and delightful sight! They freeze and form ice pillars, statues and icicles. This is something incredible! It's like time has stopped here. Everything here is special - the majesty of the mountains, the power of the river, the beauty of waterfalls, the sound of water, clean air, the greenery of the forest and serene tranquility.\r\n\r\nOn this tour, we suggest walking along the Chegem Gorge, admiring the Big and Small Chegem waterfalls, having lunch in a cafe and trying the local cuisine. Half a day is allotted for the excursion, then we return to Nalchik.\r\n\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Chegem waterfalls\"] Visit card of the Kabardino-Balkarian Republic. The waterfalls, comfortably located in the gorge of the Chegem canyon, attract many tourists and amaze everyone with their power and beauty. This is an incredibly amazing and rarest spectacle in its beauty.\r\n\r\nThe first stop of our tour is at the Big Chegem waterfalls. Directly from the steep rocks, a raging and noisy stream breaks down jets of water at high speed, forming a cascade. Some shoot out of cracks in the rock, arching in the air, falling down. Others flow in a wide stream from large holes in the rock. Falling from a great height, they break into many tiny splashes, and the sun's rays form small rainbows in them. In winter, the waterfall freezes and is simply an incredible sight! These are ice pillars, of enormous height, resembling giant candles! Some of them hang over the river with an openwork ice fringe. It's just amazing! Some kind of natural monument.\r\n\r\nChegem waterfalls are beautiful all year round. They always have their own, unique beauty and zest. The gorge has a special microclimate, due to the increased humidity from the waterfalls and river flowi",
