    "badge": "",
    "description": "Vladikavkaz, an amazingly beautiful city located in a picturesque place at the foot of the rocky mountains. It originates from the reign of Catherine II, when, according to her decree, a fortress was built between Russia and Georgia. The point was called Vladikavkaz - \"Own the Caucasus.\" The Ossetian name of this place is Dzaudzhikau - \"settlement of Dzauga\", named after the founder of the village, which appeared before the construction of the city of Dzaug Bulugov.\r\n\r\nVladikavkaz is not only mountains and Ossetian pies, it is beautiful landscapes, rich history, architectural monuments, favorable climate, tradition and culture of local residents. There are many mineral springs nearby. The capital of North Ossetia-Alania is a small, cozy, ancient town, from each window of which a chain of the Caucasus Mountains is visible. The modest beauty of Vladikavkaz will surely captivate all its guests.\r\n\r\nDeparture from Nalchik at 9:00 from city center.\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Sunni Mosque in Vladikavkaz\"]\r\n\r\nSunni mosque in Vladikavkaz  is a visiting card of Vladikavkaz.\r\n\r\nThe red-blue building against the backdrop of mountain peaks attracts tourists with its oriental beauty. According to historians, the Muslim temple is a gift from a Baku oilman to his Ossetian wife. The best craftsmen took part in the construction. For two years, the mosque was painted with sacred symbols. Thanks to its beautiful stained-glass windows, walls painted with sayings from the Koran, ornaments, the mosque resembles a precious box. The Sunni mosque is a unique creation with a rich, exquisite interior decoration, a real symbol of the city and an architectural monument of federal significance.\r\n\r\nThe place where the mosque is located is luxurious. The tops of the mountains, the handsome river Terek, and the slender, sophisticated mosque - tourists are happy to take pictures of this breathtaking beauty.\r\n\r\nIn Soviet times, the mosque was almost demolished. But the building was recaptured and the historical monument managed to be preserved. For some time, a museum of nature was organized in it, but now prayer services have been resumed again. To date, the Sunni mosque is the only functioning Muslim temple in the city.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"6694,6695,6693\"]\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"Memorial of Glory\"]\r\n\r\nMemorial of Gloryin Vladikavkaz - was opened on the 60th anniversary of the victory over Nazi Germany, in honor of the dead residents ",
