    "description": "Mountainous Adygea is a breathtaking place!\r\n\r\nA place that delights and surprises! Having been here, it seems that no one will remain indifferent!\r\n\r\nProgram :\r\n\r\nDeparture from Nalchik at 05:00 in a comfortable minibus. We are going first through Stavropol and Krasnodar regions. Then arrive to Adygea Republic. The road takes 6 hours.\r\n\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Rufabgo waterfalls\"]\r\n\r\nFirst stop Rufabgo gorge, walking tour to Rufabgo waterfalls.\r\n\r\nRufabgo waterfalls are located on the territory of Adygea and are known far beyond its borders. Waterfalls are one of the most interesting sights of the Western Caucasus, they are located near the village of Khadzhokh. The Rufabgo River formed the waterfalls of the same name, attracting crowds of tourists from all over Russia. The most famous of them are the waterfalls \"Heart of Rufabgo\", \"Noise\", \"Lace\" as well as the waterfalls \"Cascade\", \"Girl's Braids\", \"Bowl of Love\" and others. To admire the cascades of the Rufabgo waterfalls, you will have to pay for crossing the bridge leading to the waterfalls. The cost is 500 rubles per person.\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter a walk and memorable photos, we will go by minibus further to the famous Azish cave.\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"Azish cave\"]\r\n\r\nThe cave has been known since 1911, but only in 1987 it was equipped as an excursion object. The Big Azish Cave has a length of more than 640 m. Of these, 220 m of the cave are equipped for excursions. The cave consists of voluminous multi-tiered galleries and large halls. In beauty and grandeur, it surpasses many of the underground complexes. The cave is equipped with footpaths, stairs and fences, convenient and safe for inspection. There is electric lighting.\r\n\r\nThe cave is located among the beech-fir forest in the southern part of the Azish-Tau ridge. The entrance to the cavity is a vertical well. This is a hole formed as a result of the collapse of part of the roof of the upper hall. The entrance hall is the top floor of the cavity. Two more levels stand out clearly. At the bottom of the lowest passage, a stream flows, at the end of the gallery falling from a waterfall ledge and disappearing in narrow crevices a few more meters later.\r\n\r\nThe entrance to the cave must be paid.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAnd the end point of the tour will be the journey to the Lago-Naki Plateau.\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"3\" title=\"Plateau Lago-Naki\"]\r\nThe Lago-Naki plateau is located between two ri",
