    "description": "Abai-Su is the highest non-cascade waterfall in Kabardino-Balkaria. The name of the waterfall was given in honor of the well-aimed hunter Abai. This natural attraction of the republic is very popular. Every year hundreds of tourists from all over the country come here to look at this unique creation of nature.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"3400,3371,3390\"]\r\n\r\nA beautiful, powerful, noisy waterfall seems to be pouring straight from the depths of the rock, falling down with incredible force. The waterfall flows into the lake. Abai-Su does not have cascades, it descends not in a single stream, but in a huge number of streams that run along the stone ledges, either connecting together or splitting into parts. You can spend hours admiring the beauty of falling water, its diversity and strength.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"3393,3373,3368\"]\r\n\r\nIn winter, the waterfall completely freezes. As if time stops with it. An ice sculpture appears before tourists. This is an incredible sight. The radiance of stalactites and stalagmites under the winter sun gives all tourists amazing emotions. In warm winters, only the bottom of the waterfall freezes, and then the picture becomes completely amazing - the water from above is poured in a continuous stream like into an ice glass.\r\nTour program\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Chegem waterfalls\"]\r\nIn the tour program we will visit one of the main attractions of the republic - Chegem waterfalls. Let's admire how the noisy streams of water break into the steep cliffs of the picturesque gorge. Some of which flow down from the round holes of the rocks, some fall from a height in a wide water ribbon and breaking on stone ledges, break up into billions of water splashes.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"1927,1930,1916\"]\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"The village of El-Tyubu\"]\r\nWe will visit the ancient mountain village of El-Tubyu. This is a necropolis, the buildings of which are dated from the 10th to the 17th century. During the construction of the modern village, the remains of older buildings were preserved. Here the present meets the past. Everywhere reigns the aura of antiquity. Some stone houses are several hundred years old.\r\n\r\nIn the very center there is an ancient medieval tower, which was built by eminent masters for the Balkarukov princes in the 17th - 18th centuries.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"3376,3375,3367\"]\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"3\" title=\"Paragliding in Chegem\"]\r\n\r\nThe Chegem canyon, mountains, ",
