    "description": "The first part of the trip is described here - Jeep tour in Cherek-Balkaria canyon\r\n\r\nLake Giybashkel is located in the Cherek Gorge above 3000 meters above sea level. The road to it starts from the village of Upper Balkaria. Further - only on foot, about 6 km along the valley of the Chainashki River. The landscape is unusual, as if from The Lord of the Rings. There are also peacefully grazing horses, and wild yaks, and eagles soaring overhead.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"4263,4258,4249,4268,4266,4265\"]\r\n\r\nWe drive up to the upper kosh (farm yard) in the upper reaches of river Chainashki. Our walking path to the Giy-Bash-Kol Lake begins from the upper reaches of the Chainashki gorge, from the upper kosh, where the road ends, almost ending on the majestic mountain range of Kayashki-Su-Bashi, from which a picturesque waterfall falls right in front of us, and a glacier shines above. And here we are crossing the Chaynashki River and heading to the old and almost invisible geological road, which will lead us in a steep serpentine to the Turashashki gorge. New views, new experiences!\r\n\r\nOn the left rises the rocky peak of Suuk-Auz-Kaya, closer to us is the peak of Rechitebe, from which there is a mountain range with small peaks and passes, behind one of which our lake is located. The path through the gorge is not difficult, but the height is already felt, snow can fall on the path even in summer. An hour's journey and we are approaching the pass take-off. This is a steep ascent of 150 meters, snowy until mid-July, later it is a scree path leading in a steep zigzag to the Turashashki pass. The trek to the pass offers an indescribable view of the Sugan mountain range, or, as it is also called, the Sugan Alps. But let's look a little lower and in front of us is a turquoise expanse of water, quite close. We go down 50 meters - and we are on the shore of the lake!\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"4254,4253,4252\"]\r\n\r\nHere we will make a basic rest with hot meals, photography, those who wish can go to the second lake, which is lower. After that we will go back.\r\nIn these places, in addition to beauty, you can meet herds of yaks, very unusual animals. Or to see how the Turashashki River originates, flowing out from under the stones, and then, instead of flowing in the depths of the gorge, it runs along its edge, over the discharge into the Chainashki gorge! Amazing place.\r\n\r\n\r\nTour program\n\n\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Departure\"]Transfer on 4 wheel car from Nalchik at 7:00",
