    "description": "Tour briefly\r\nFrom Nalchik we leave to Elbrus area by minibus. In 2 hours we will be at the village of Elbrus.\r\n\r\nWe are going to an amazing route in the Irik-Chat gorge to the pass of the same name. It will start immediately with a steep climb up the grassy path. The climb is difficult, but small, be sure to take care of comfortable shoes. At the top we will see the beauty of the snowy peaks of the Caucasus Mountains. Further along the flat area we will go to the Narzan spring, near which we will make our first halt. Having rested, we will start the second difficult ascent along the scree path. Past the Sandcastle, we will come to a pine forest. Finally, we again have a flat slope, we will make a halt, rest after the ascent. Here, tourists take gorgeous photos, because the views around are very picturesque. Further we are going for a long transition through the forest to the lower pass. There we settle down for a substantial lunch and decide where we will go next.\r\n\r\n[gallery columns=\"1\" size=\"medium\" ids=\"6027\"]\r\n\r\nAfter resting for an hour, we will start climbing a steep serpentine along a grassy slope to the Gorge Irik. There, at an altitude of 4000 m, we will see mountain peaks right in front of us and admire the silvery mountain rivers Irik and Chat, forest, glacial moraine from a dizzying height. Or we can go to the Irik gorge to the Irik-Chat pass.\r\n\r\nWe set off to the village of Elbrus, where the transfer will take us back to Nalchik.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"4485,4486,4487,4488,4489,4490\"]\r\nTour Program\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Departure to the Elbrus region\"] Our trip to the Irik gorge and to the Irik-Chat pass will start from the village of Elbrus. The first ascent will be steep and rather difficult, along a scree path. After a short ascent, we will go out onto the plain and we will have a gorgeous view of the snow caps of the mountain peaks. Seeing this beauty, you will immediately forget about the hard ascent. Then we will pass along a fairly flat area to the Narzan spring, here we will make the first halt. After resting, we will proceed to the second steep ascent, past the Sandcastle to the edge of the pine forest.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"4478,4482,4483\"]\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"4480,4481,4484\"]\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"Hiking Route\"]As a reward for passing this section, we will see a picturesque gentle slope and make a second halt for rest. You can have a little refreshment, take memorable p",
