    "description": "Two countries - one trip - Armenia + Georgia.\r\n\r\nDeparture from airport Mineralnye Vody at daytime to Yerevan.\r\n\r\nIt is possible to purchase a tour with an independent arrival in Yerevan with an additional charge for a meeting and transfer from airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n[timeline]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"1\" title=\"Day 1\"]\r\n\r\nDeparture from MinVody airport, but it is possible to purchase a tour with independent arrival in Yerevan.\r\n\r\nArrival in Yerevan. Accommodation at the hotel in the center of Yerevan.\r\n\r\nFree time.\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"2\" title=\"Day 2\"]\r\n\r\nBreakfast\r\nKhor Virap\r\nDeparture for an excursion to the monastery Khor Virap (Deep Pit)\r\n\r\nThe monastery is located at the very border of Armenia with Turkey, on a hill, in the vicinity of the village of Pokr Vedi. In ancient times, the city of Artashat, the ancient capital of Armenia, was located on this territory. This fortress monastery is a place of pilgrimage, one of the most revered places in Armenia, sacred to the Armenian Apostolic Church. The monastery was erected in the period from the 6th to the 17th centuries, above the dungeon where the baptist of Armenia, St. Gregory, languished.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"6214,6218,6219,6212,6217,6215\"]\r\n\r\nTransfer to the city Etchmiadzin - the center of the Armenian Apostolic Church. Inspection of the Cathedral in Etchmiadzin - the main church in Armenia, which is called the Mother Church.\r\n\r\nLunch (not included)\r\nYerevan city tour \r\nVisit to the Mother Armenia monument. A complex dedicated to the victory in the Great Patriotic War. On the territory of the complex there is a statue of Mother Armenia, a symbol of the country.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"6238,6252,6253\"]\r\n\r\nCascade Complex is an impressive staircase complex that connects 2 districts of Yerevan. Now on the territory of the complex there is an open-air museum, where the works of contemporary artists and sculptors are presented.\r\n\r\nThe building of the Opera and Ballet Theatre is a unique building built of gray tuff and includes elements of traditional architecture.\r\n\r\n[gallery ids=\"6209,6240,6221,6210,6260,6259\"]\r\n\r\nAbovyan Street is a very colorful street where historical buildings built in the early 20th century are located.\r\n\r\nRepublic Square - The heart of Yerevan.\r\n\r\nThe complex Tsitsernakaberd is a memorial dedicated to the victims of the Armenian Genocide in the Ottoman Empire.\r\n\r\n[/timeline_item]\r\n[timeline_item item_number=\"3\" title=\"Day 3\"]\r\n\r\nBreakfast\r\n\r\nDeparture for the Tour ",
